.TH TCMP 1.SH NAMEtcmp \- compare two text files.SH SYNOPSIS\fBtcmp\fR[\-s\fIdd\fR] [\-f\fInnnn\fR] [\-t\fInnnn\fR] file1 file2.SH DESCRIPTION\fBtcmp\fRreads two text files side by side and reports each difference as theline numbers in both files, then the line as each has it:.nf    > Line 2 of f1 changed to line 2 of f2    two    TWO.fi.PPWhen lines are added or removed it looks ahead to find where the twofiles agree again, and carries on from there.  A line that differs onlyin tabs and spaces counts as changed..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s\fIdd\fRlook up to\fIdd\fRlines ahead to resynchronise; 3 unless told, and\fB\-s0\fRcompares strictly line against line..TP 12\fB\-f\fInnnn\fRstart at line\fInnnn\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-t\fInnnn\fRstop at line\fInnnn\fR.\fR.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOdiff, cmp